      "settings": {
        "image_alt": "Kapok fiber close-up",
        "badge_text": "100% Natural Fill",
        "label": "The Material Story",
        "title": "<p>Kapok: Nature's gift, rediscovered.</p>",
        "description": "Kapok is a silky fiber harvested from the tropical Ceiba tree — one of Earth's most ancient insulators. Revered in Asia for centuries, kapok is naturally hollow, trapping air like tiny insulating bubbles. The result: extraordinary warmth with almost no weight.\n\nUnlike down, kapok is vegan and hypoallergenic. Unlike synthetic fills, kapok is 100% biodegradable and requires no chemicals to grow. It's warmth the planet actually approves of."
      }
